cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Phobos in your work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Phobos"
abstract: >-
  Phobos is a sandboxing solution for programming exercises on interactive learning
  platforms. An offline pruning phase discovers the minimal set of files and network
  hosts a test run actually needs, by iteratively hiding directories and observing which
  runs break. Student submissions then execute under Landlock, an unprivileged Linux kernel
  sandbox, with access to only that allow-list and to the TCP ports it names. Outbound
  connections are supervised from outside the process by a seccomp-based connect guard,
  which enforces the allow-list by host and port, and a rule that names a host is enforced by
  an optional egress broker that checks the TLS host name, so that undeclared network access
  fails. A timeout and resource limits bound the run.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ls1intum/phobos"
